+### Duration
+
+{class}`Duration` converts a string into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. It accepts either a whole number of seconds,
+such as `120`, or one or more `<integer><unit>` groups using the units `d`, `h`, `m` and `s`, such as `2d`, `1h30m` or
+`1d2h3m4s`. Each unit may appear at most once, in that order, with no spaces. Matching is case-insensitive.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30m")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(timeout)
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+```
+
